			"widgets_values":[
				"subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is a common domestic short-haired cat, agile, quick reflexes, with playful aggressive teasing behavior.\n<Subject 2> is a cockatiel with yellow head crest, orange circular cheek patches, light gray plumage, tiny fragile body, timid personality.\n<Subject 3> is an adult human in casual home loungewear, holding a cloth slipper for one single throw action.\nsummary:\n[reference generation] 10-second vertical short video. A house cat bullies a cockatiel on indoor living room floor. A human witnesses the scene, throws one slipper once to scare the cat, the slipper misses the cat, hits the cockatiel directly and knocks it unconscious, the cat flees out of frame instantly.\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2], [Shot 3]): fully_preserved - cat’s feline appearance, harassing paw taps, rapid escape dash are fully retained.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2], [Shot 3]): fully_preserved - cockatiel’s signature crest, orange cheek spots, frightened fluttering, limp unconscious state after impact fully retained.\n<Subject 3> (appears in [Shot 2], [Shot 3]): fully_preserved - human’s casual home outfit, one single slipper-throwing motion, shocked remorseful facial expression fully retained.\ndetailed_description:\nVideo overall specs: 9:16 vertical, total runtime 00:10.000, bright warm daily home realistic style, soft natural indoor window lighting, smooth short-video handheld camera language.\n[Shot 1] 00:00.000–00:03.000, medium shot, frame living room wooden floor. <Subject 1> creeps low toward stationary <Subject 2>, taps the cockatiel’s wings and crest repeatedly with front paws, blocks the bird’s escape path. <Subject 2> flutters small wings nervously, lets out soft scared chirps, cowers on floor with nowhere to hide. Off-screen, <Subject 3> approaches and watches the bullying scene.\n[Shot 2] At 00:03.000, cut to medium shot focusing on <Subject 3>. Human’s eyes widen upon seeing the cat’s harassment, bends down to grab one cloth slipper, pulls arm back to prepare one single throw only, no repeated swings. <Subject 1> senses danger, tenses limbs ready to run, stays between human and cockatiel.\n[Shot 3] At 00:05.000, dynamic tracking close-up, lasts until 00:10.000. <Subject 3> releases slipper in one single throwing motion. <Subject 1> leaps sideways instantly and scampers fully out of camera frame. The flying slipper slams straight into <Subject 2>’s torso. Cockatiel lets out one sharp short squawk, body immediately goes limp, wings fold loose, lies motionless flat on floor fully knocked unconscious. <Subject 3> freezes in throw follow-through posture, stares blankly at the unconscious parrot with obvious stunned guilt, camera holds this tragic funny ending frame till video ends at 10 seconds.\noverall_soundscape:\nContinuous faint quiet indoor room background hum; soft hissing from cat while teasing bird; thin frightened chirps of cockatiel; quick whoosh airflow sound of thrown slipper; dull heavy thud impact when slipper hits parrot; one brief pained squawk from cockatiel; fast rustling paw sounds as cat sprints away; quiet shocked gasp from human.\nnon_diegetic_music:\nLight casual acoustic guitar background melody, slow gentle tempo, no loud dramatic swells, light comedic slightly awkward atmosphere matching the accident plot."
